      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Disclosed herein is an unprecedented cobalt-catalyzed trifluoromethylation-peroxidation of unactivated alkenes. In this process the hydroperoxide acts as a radical initiator as well as a coupling partner. The cheap and readily available sodium trifluoromethanesulfinate serves as the CF3 source in the reaction. Various alkenes are transformed into vicinal trifluoromethyl-peroxide compounds in moderate to good yields."},
